@* Password recovery, which is two routes rather than two client-side steps: /reset asks for
   the address, /reset/sent says so. Each is a real URL, so the back button behaves and a
   refresh does not resubmit.

   The response is deliberately the same whether or not the address exists. Saying "no such
   account" turns the form into a way of asking whether someone has one. *@

<div class="flex min-h-[60vh] items-center justify-center">
    <Card Class="w-full max-w-sm">
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Reset your password</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>
                We will send a link to the address on the account.
            </CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>

        <form method="post" action="/reset" class="reset-form" up-target=".reset-form">
            <CardContent>
                <FormField For="rp-email" Label="Email">
                    <Input id="rp-email" name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="username" />
                </FormField>
            </CardContent>

            <CardFooter Class="mt-6 flex-col gap-3">
                <Button Class="w-full" up-disable>Send the link</Button>
                <a href="/login" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
                    Back to sign in
                </a>
            </CardFooter>
        </form>
    </Card>
</div>
